{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Working with Quantity","role":"article"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create, convert, compare, compute with, and format "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" values in your app."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/workingwithquantity"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the type you’ll reach for most often. It works the way"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"Foundation’s "},{"code":"Measurement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does, but with compile-time dimension checking: a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quantity always knows its unit, and its unit knows its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This article covers everything you can do with a quantity, grouped the same way","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Apple documents its own value types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Create-a-Quantity","type":"heading","text":"Create a Quantity"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a quantity with a value and a unit using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/init(value:unit:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Math","","\/\/ Distance","let jumpLength = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.meter)","","\/\/ Money — currency units place their symbol before the value ($8.95)","let price = Quantity(value: 8.95, unit: Units.usd)","","\/\/ Temperature — offset units like Celsius convert correctly","let bodyTemp = Quantity(value: 37.0, unit: Units.celsius)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The value is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so you can pass integer literals directly:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Quantity(value: 42, unit: Units.kilometer)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Convert Between Units","anchor":"Convert-Between-Units"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/converted(to:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to convert to another unit of the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension. The framework converts through the unit’s base unit, so arbitrary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chains like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nanometer → kilometer"},{"type":"text","text":" just work:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let chipFeature = Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.nanometer)","let inMeters = chipFeature.converted(to: Units.meter)","print(inMeters.value) \/\/ 5e-09","","let marathon = Quantity(value: 42.195, unit: Units.kilometer)","print(marathon.converted(to: Units.mile).value) \/\/ 26.218...","","let paycheck = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.eur)","print(paycheck.converted(to: Units.usd).value) \/\/ 108.0"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Because conversions require matching dimensions, converting a ","type":"text"},{"code":"length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" doesn’t compile (or traps at runtime if the units are fully dynamic).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for details.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Compare Quantities","anchor":"Compare-Quantities","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Quantities of the same unit type compare by their values with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":". To compare"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quantities expressed in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" units of the same dimension—or to allow a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"small tolerance—use ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/isEquivalent(to:tolerance:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let oneMile = Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.mile)","let oneKm    = Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.kilometer)","","oneMile.isEquivalent(to: Quantity(value: 1609.344, unit: Units.meter)) \/\/ true","oneMile.isEquivalent(to: oneKm)                                        \/\/ false"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Add and Subtract Quantities","anchor":"Add-and-Subtract-Quantities"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can add and subtract quantities of the same dimension even when their units"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differ. The result keeps the left-hand side’s unit; the right-hand side is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converted automatically:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let dish = Quantity(value: 1.5, unit: Units.kilogram)","let spice = Quantity(value: 350.0, unit: Units.gram)","","let total = dish + spice","print(total) \/\/ 1.85 kg"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Multiply and Divide Quantities","anchor":"Multiply-and-Divide-Quantities"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Multiplying or dividing two quantities combines their dimensions and produces a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompositeUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The framework adjusts both the numeric value and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"coefficient so results stay physically correct:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let area = Quantity(value: 3.0, unit: Units.meter) * Quantity(value: 2.0, unit: Units.meter)","print(area.value)          \/\/ 6.0","print(area.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"(m*m)\"","print(area.unit.dimension) \/\/ area","","let speed = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.meter) \/ Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.second)","print(speed.value)          \/\/ 20.0","print(speed.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"(m\/s)\"","print(speed.unit.dimension) \/\/ speed"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also multiply and divide a quantity by a plain "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" scalar, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the same unit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let doubling = Quantity(value: 5.0, unit: Units.meter) * 2","print(doubling) \/\/ 10.00 m"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For common derived dimensions, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" produces cleaner units. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiplying a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/power","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/time","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" yields an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"energy unit with the conventional symbol ordering:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let power   = Quantity(value: 2.0, unit: Units.kilowatt)","let runTime = Quantity(value: 3.0, unit: Units.hour)","let energy  = power * runTime    \/\/ 6 kWh, dimension = energy"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Format Quantities","anchor":"Format-Quantities"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"type":"text","text":", so it prints a formatted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"string automatically. Use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity\/formatted(decimalPlaces:includeSpace:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to control the decimal places and spacing. Currency symbols are placed before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the value by default; most other symbols follow it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let tenDollars = Quantity(value: 10.1234, unit: Units.usd)","print(tenDollars.formatted())                 \/\/ \"$10.12\"","print(tenDollars.formatted(decimalPlaces: 3)) \/\/ \"$10.123\"","","let fiveMeters = Quantity(value: 5.5, unit: Units.meter)","print(fiveMeters.formatted())                 \/\/ \"5.50 m\"","print(fiveMeters.formatted(includeSpace: false)) \/\/ \"5.50m\"","","let percent = Quantity(value: 75.5, unit: Units.percent)","print(percent.formatted())                    \/\/ \"75.5%\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"What’s Next?","anchor":"Whats-Next"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the ready-made units in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or define your own named units with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Build composite units dynamically by combining units with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operators defined for "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to define units for your own domain.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to make dimension correctness a compile-time","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarantee.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/WorkingWithQuantity","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/StoringAndEncodingQuantities","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitsByDimension","doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity"],"anchor":"Essentials"}],"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/StoringAndEncodingQuantities":{"title":"Storing and Encoding Quantities","kind":"articl